  ('2.4.7', 'There is a visible indicator for page elements when they receive keyboard focus.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.8', 'If a web page is part of a sequence of pages or within a complex site structure, an indication of the current page location is provided, for example, through breadcrumbs or specifying the current step in a sequence (e.g., "Step 2 of 5 - Shipping Address").', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.9', 'Links that have identical accessible names point to the same destination, ensuring that identical link text does not lead to different locations.', 'axe-core', 'identical-links-same-purpose'),
  ('2.4.9', 'Each link’s text alone clearly and accurately describes its purpose without relying on surrounding context.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.9', 'Image links, image buttons, and image map hotspots have text alternatives that clearly convey their purpose.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.9', 'Link text is meaningful, descriptive, and not vague (for example, avoiding “click here” or “more”).', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.9', 'Links that appear visually similar but have different purposes are clearly differentiated by their text.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.9', 'The purpose of links remains clear when presented out of visual context (for example, in a list of links).', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.10', 'Headings follow a logical and hierarchical order without skipping heading levels.', 'axe-core', '- heading-order (partial)'),
  ('2.4.10', 'All meaningful sections of content are identified using headings where appropriate.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.10', 'Headings accurately describe the content or purpose of their respective sections.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.10', 'Headings are used consistently to organize content and improve navigability.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.10', 'Headings are not used solely for visual styling purposes.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.4.10', 'Section headings remain meaningful when accessed via assistive technology (e.g., headings list).', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.1', 'If multipoint or path-based gestures (such as pinching, swiping, or dragging across the screen) are not essential to the functionality, then the functionality can also be performed with a single point activation (such as activating a button).', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.2', 'To help avoid inadvertent activation of controls, avoid non-essential down-event (e.g., onmousedown) activation when clicking, tapping, or long pressing the screen.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.2', 'Use onclick, onmouseup, or similar instead.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.2', 'If onmouseup (or similar) is used, you must provide a mechanism to abort or undo the action performed.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.3', 'The accessible name of an interactive component contains the visible text presented to users.', 'axe-core', 'label-content-name-mismatch'),
  ('2.5.3', 'The accessible name includes the visible text in the same order and without altering its meaning.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.3', 'Accessible names derived from aria-label or aria-labelledby accurately reflect the visible label text.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.3', 'Image buttons and icons with visible text equivalents include that text in the accessible name.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.3', 'Dynamic changes to visible labels are reflected in the accessible name.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.3', 'Abbreviations or symbols used visually are appropriately represented in the accessible name.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.4', 'Functionality that is triggered by moving the device (such as shaking or panning a mobile device) or by user movement (such as waving to a camera) can be disabled and equivalent functionality is provided via standard controls like buttons.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.5', 'Clickable targets are at least 44 by 44 pixels in size unless an alternative target of that size is provided, the target is inline (such as a link within a sentence), the target is not author-modified (such as a default checkbox), or the small target size is essential to the functionality.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('2.5.6', 'Content does not require a specific input type, such as touch-only or keyboard-only, but must support alternative inputs (such as using a keyboard on a mobile device).', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.1', 'The <html> element includes a valid and non-empty lang attribute.', 'axe-core', 'html-has-lang, html-lang-valid'),
  ('3.1.1', 'The lang attribute value correctly identifies the primary language of the page content.', 'axe-core', 'html-xml-lang-mismatch'),
  ('3.1.1', 'The language declared in the lang attribute matches the actual language used throughout the page.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.1', 'The language declaration remains accurate when page content or locale changes dynamically.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.2', 'Elements with a lang attribute use a valid language code according to BCP', 'axe-core', 'valid-lang'),
  ('3.1.2', '47.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.2', 'All passages of content written in a different language from the primary page language are correctly identified using the lang attribute.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.2', 'The language specified in the lang attribute accurately matches the language of the content.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.2', 'Language changes are applied consistently to all relevant text segments (including dynamically generated content).', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.2', 'Nested language changes are correctly marked when multiple languages appear within the same content block.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.3', 'Words that may be ambiguous, unfamiliar, or used in a very specific way are defined through adjacent text, a definition list, a glossary, or other suitable method.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.4', 'The meaning of an unfamiliar abbreviation is provided by expanding it the first time it is used, using the <abbr> element, or linking to a definition or glossary.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.5', 'A more understandable alternative is provided for content that is more advanced than can be reasonably read by a person with roughly 9 years of primary education.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.1.6', 'If the pronunciation of a word is vital to understanding that word, its pronunciation is provided immediately following the word or via a link or glossary', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.2.1', 'When a page element receives focus, it does not result in a substantial change to the page, the spawning of a pop-up window, an additional change of keyboard focus, or any other change that could confuse or disorient the user.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.2.2', 'When a user inputs information or interacts with a control, it does not result in a substantial change to the page, the spawning of a pop-up window, an additional change of keyboard focus, or any other change that could confuse or disorient the user unless the user is informed of the change ahead of time.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.2.3', 'Navigation links that are repeated on web pages do not change order when navigating through the site', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.2.4', 'Elements that have the same functionality across multiple web pages are consistently identified.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.2.4', 'For example, a search box at the top of the site should always be labeled the same way.', 'manual', NULL),
  ('3.2.5', 'Substantial changes to the page, the spawning of pop-up windows, uncontrolled changes of keyboard focus, or any other change that could confuse or disorient the user must be initiated by the user.', 'manual', NULL),
